  "prefLabel": "Fis 2001.01 Chapter Definitions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Fis 2001.01 Chapter Definitions.\n\n(a) “Commercial qualifying years” means the 2010 through 2013 multispecies fishing years for NOAA Fisheries permit owners. A multispecies fishing year runs from May 1 through April 30.\n\n(b) “Direct assistance” means the funds supplied by the Greater Atlantic Fisheries Disaster Direct Assistance Program and distributed to NE Multispecies permitted vessels in 2014.\n\n(c) “For-hire qualifying years” means the calendar years of 2010 through 2013 for the For-Hire industry.\n\n(d) “Individual” means a natural person or business.\n\n(e) “NE multispecies groundfish” means the following northeast groundfish: American plaice, Atlantic cod, haddock, pollock, redfish, white hake, winter flounder, witch flounder, and yellowtail flounder.\n\n(f) “Program” refers to the New Hampshire Greater Atlantic Fisheries Disaster State- Specific Assistance Program.\n\nSource. #10846, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 6-5-15, EXPIRES: 12-2-15",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/fis2000.html"
}
